    "answer": {
      "short": "$99\\,999$, for example. Rounding to the nearest ten thousand, thousand, hundred or ten gives $100\\,000$.",
      "worked": "One possible number is $99\\,999$.\n\nFor this number, 1, 2, 3 and 4 significant figures correspond respectively to rounding to the nearest ten thousand, thousand, hundred and ten. Each rounds up:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}99\\,999&\\approx100\\,000\\quad(1\\text{ s.f.})\\\\99\\,999&\\approx100\\,000\\quad(2\\text{ s.f.})\\\\99\\,999&\\approx100\\,000\\quad(3\\text{ s.f.})\\\\99\\,999&\\approx100\\,000\\quad(4\\text{ s.f.})\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
